WEBVTT

1
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.200
<i>Cop stops you at a roadblock
Takes all your papers away</i>

2
00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:24.160
<i>Give him license registration
Want ’em back, now you gotta pay</i>

3
00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:30.170
<i>Son of a General, speeding drunk
in his Porsche Cayenne</i>

4
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.550
<i>Hit a farmer on the highway
Push the speed, two hundred and ten</i>

5
00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:41.300
<i>I’m so bored with Morocco</i>

6
00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.230
<i>But what can I do?</i>

7
00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:58.030
<i>Maghrib nouveaux riches:
Just a bunch of fucking hoods</i>

8
00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:03.370
<i>Village in a forest, kick the people out
Cut it down and sell the wood</i>

9
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:08.710
<i>Down the alley come four police
Beat you here or at the station</i>

10
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:14.380
<i>Next day body parts on the ground
Or you’re gone to your final destination</i>

11
00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.300
It should be faster, come on.

12
00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:21.180
Norah, get into it.
Punk rock, okay?

13
00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.890
Don’t let it drag.

14
00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:28.350
Are you ready?
Sarah, Bonnie, Basma?

15
00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.600
Let’s go. One, two, three.

16
00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:44.620
<i>Maghrib politicians
Here comes election day</i>

17
00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:51.210
<i>Slogans lies empty promises
Don’t believe a word they say</i>

18
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:57.130
<i>What a country: Sun, Sea and Sand
And all of us burning to get out</i>

19
00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:01.380
<i>Émigré washed up on the coast of Spain
Or in prison cause he got sold out</i>

20
00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.640
Fatima?

21
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.850
Malika? What are you doing here?

22
00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:12.190
Why are you out so late?

23
00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.360
Waiting for the bus.

24
00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:15.440
Come on, get in.

25
00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.440
We’ll give you a ride home.

26
00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:24.370
<i>Morocco’s rich now let’s go
spend 2 billion Euros on a high speed train</i>

27
00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:29.250
<i>Meanwhile in the ghetto
People have nothing to eat</i>

28
00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.790
More, more.

29
00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:35.420
<i>Welcome to our hospital
Don’t even have antiseptic</i>

30
00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:40.090
<i>You walk in sick or wounded
They carry you out to the funeral home</i>

31
00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.170
Shit, the cops.

32
00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.760
Turn everything off now!

33
00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:49.970
Calm down, be cool.

34
00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.520
Good evening, papers please.

35
00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.080
Basma, deal with him.

36
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.750
There goes the rest of our money.

37
00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:36.400
Malika, will you take me
to a real concert sometime?

38
00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.320
<i>Insha’Allah.</i> But listen,
about what you saw tonight...

39
00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.400
I won’t say anything, don’t worry.

40
00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:47.370
Can you make money from doing music?

41
00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:51.370
If you’re good enough...

42
00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.370
and work your ass off...

43
00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.920
and are lucky.

44
00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.300
Even then, 99 musicians
out of a hundred fail.

45
00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:07.010
You’re going away, aren’t you?

46
00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:11.640
That’s what your video is for, right?
Leaving.

47
00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.270
You know, we sent some songs
to this producer.

48
00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:20.230
If she likes it... we might go
make an album. Go on tour.

49
00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.490
If you leave,
you won’t come back.

50
00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.450
Slow down.

51
00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:34.410
I don’t have a ticket anywhere!
I said “if” the producer likes the songs.

52
00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.670
If you leave, you won’t come back.

53
00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:03.960
Good morning.

54
00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.470
Where were you two last night?
I don’t want to hear a lie.

55
00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.390
Well, I found her at the bus stop.

56
00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:17.520
I had to work late,
I couldn’t pick her up.

57
00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.310
Good-bye.

58
00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:33.110
Sir, this is Caroline from Francecom.
I am calling you with an exceptional offer.

59
00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.660
It’s a holiday package with–

60
00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:42.620
I understand, sir, but the offer
is available for 18 months.

61
00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:48.000
Yes, my name is Caroline.

62
00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:52.130
Accent? Which accent?

63
00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.180
You have an accent too. I think
it’s from the south of France, right?

64
00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:58.060
You donkey.

65
00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.520
Let’s go, Missy.

66
00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.110
There are 250 other Carolines
like you waiting for your job.

67
00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:26.170
- Fired?
- Yep.

68
00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:27.630
Fucking Frenchy asshole!

69
00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:29.840
Don’t be a racist.

70
00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:33.170
Let’s sweeten the deal a little.

71
00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:37.470
Watch my back.

72
00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:53.400
See you at practice.

73
00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.710
What?

74
00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:12.840
It’s Jade. She wants to meet me.

75
00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.300
Awesome!

76
00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.550
Calm down.

77
00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.810
- So what are you doing? Call her!
- She wants to meet tonight.

78
00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.890
Call her now!

79
00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.800
Malika? Good evening!

80
00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.670
- I’m pleased to meet you.
- Me too.

81
00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:00.140
I really liked “I’m so bored with Morocco.”

82
00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:02.010
It’s really good.

83
00:10:02.760 --> 00:10:04.970
There’s a political punch.

84
00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:07.060
Old school. I love it.

85
00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:09.270
Thanks.

86
00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.860
You a fan of Joe Strummer?

87
00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:13.820
Yes.

88
00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.490
Well, you have one thing
in common with him:

89
00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.860
you both sing like crap.

90
00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:24.700
It’s a joke!

91
00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.540
Listen, I’m going to London.

92
00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:32.000
I will be back in two weeks.

93
00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:34.880
And then we’ll try
to record a demo together.

94
00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:38.050
Okay?

95
00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.640
You’re The Traitors, right?

96
00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:43.510
Just Traitors.

97
00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:52.190
Reserve the Studio Alpha in Casablanca
from the 25th to the 30th.

98
00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.690
Talk to Hicham,
tell him I sent you.

99
00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:58.780
We have to pay for those five days?

100
00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.030
Of course, it’s your demo.

101
00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:06.200
You want to produce us
but we have to pay?

102
00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:10.420
I am a producer, not an ATM.

103
00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:27.720
- Hi, Malika. How are you?
- Got some work for me, by any chance?

104
00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:31.100
- Sorry, nothing now.
- Thank you.

105
00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:34.540
How are you, Dad?

106
00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.000
I’m okay.

107
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.010
I would like to come
working for three weeks.

108
00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:42.720
Not like last time.
I’ll work really hard.

109
00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:46.970
What happened to your office job?

110
00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.430
It dried up.

111
00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:56.940
Is that a new battery?

112
00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:09.830
You want money to go singing and
dancing with those street girls, right?

113
00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.950
Dad, please don’t start.

114
00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:16.670
You’re 25. No job, no husband.

115
00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.880
And you stay out
until God knows what time.

116
00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:24.260
- You know what people say about me?
- I can move out anytime you want.

117
00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:31.470
Hey! Bring that part.

118
00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:37.190
Not this. The other one.

119
00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:39.730
Can’t you see
what I’m working on?

120
00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.610
You’re not moving anywhere
till you get married.

121
00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.990
But who wants to marry
a girl who wears jeans...

122
00:13:49.070 --> 00:13:51.200
with dirty fingernails.

123
00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:54.870
Not even a butcher
wants to marry you!

124
00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:33.910
- Where’s your boss?
- He’s not here. It’s closing time.

125
00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:40.170
It’s running bad, huh?

126
00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.670
Is the motor weak
when you’re going uphill?

127
00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:46.970
Open the hood.

128
00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.390
Khalil, bring the water.

129
00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:16.830
You’ve got a problem
with the pressure screw.

130
00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:20.040
I can fix it. 500 dirhams.

131
00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.880
500? A new one costs only 50.

132
00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.920
Order it from Casablanca and see
if you can get it in 10 days.

133
00:15:29.630 --> 00:15:31.130
Fix it.

134
00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.260
Come back in four hours.

135
00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:35.220
Give me your phone.

136
00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:47.030
Call me when you’re done.

137
00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.070
Khalil, 24 socket wrench.

138
00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:05.940
Have you finished?

139
00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.770
- It’s ready.
- Is it working?

140
00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:10.980
Try it if you want.

141
00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:12.900
Omar.

142
00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.090
You’re a little badass.

143
00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.510
Too bad you dress like a boy.

144
00:17:38.050 --> 00:17:39.890
Thanks.

145
00:17:55.070 --> 00:17:57.070
Those guys are in the hash
business.

146
00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.450
Forget what you’ve seen.

147
00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:11.540
Okay, take me downtown, please.

148
00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:30.270
Hey, Bonny.

149
00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:35.650
He said no?
Listen: no money, no studio.

150
00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:39.360
Yeah, okay, I’ll find us the money.

151
00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:43.030
I’ll find the money.

152
00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:45.910
All right. Bye.

153
00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:49.790
I’m finishing work,
and you girls are just starting...

154
00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:05.810
Hey, baby.
I’m so cold and you’re so hot.

155
00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:07.810
You’re a dirty girl, dirty!

156
00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:09.600
Next time I’ll kick your ass.

157
00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:29.290
Hey, Malika.

158
00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:31.250
How’s it going?

159
00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:32.920
Fine, and you?

160
00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.250
You know, same old shit.

161
00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:38.170
To what do I owe the pleasure?
You want something?

162
00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:40.300
Yeah, I need the money you borrowed.

163
00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.180
Truth is, I just don’t have it right now.

164
00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:46.430
Come on, Jihan.
I really need that money. Please.

165
00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:50.270
Look, wait five minutes, I’ll get dressed
and we’ll go get your money, okay?

166
00:19:50.350 --> 00:19:53.190
Okay, I’ll wait. Don’t take too long.

167
00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:58.990
- Want a Red Bull? Vodka?
- No thanks.

168
00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:19.420
- I hate clubs.
- Go in, it’s not going to kill you.

169
00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:28.810
See, Adil’s here.
I’ll get you your money.

170
00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.360
What can I get you?

171
00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:44.820
A Coke.

172
00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:20.570
Hello.

173
00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:22.150
Hi.

174
00:21:23.070 --> 00:21:24.650
What are you thinking about?

175
00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:27.200
I’m thinking about a whiskey.

176
00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.450
A Johnny Red for the lady.

177
00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:33.660
Where are you from, beautiful?

178
00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:35.790
From Donkeyville.

179
00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:37.540
That’s in the South, right?

180
00:21:38.380 --> 00:21:40.300
You seem lonely.

181
00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:43.050
Very lonely.

182
00:21:45.090 --> 00:21:47.300
I could keep you company.

183
00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:49.890
Yes? I’m listening.

184
00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:51.470
You want to?

185
00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.390
Depends how much.

186
00:21:54.060 --> 00:21:56.100
2,000 for the whole night.

187
00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:01.690
I’ll give you 1600, and I don’t
pay the room or anybody else.

188
00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:03.360
But you do everything I say.

189
00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:08.280
You seem so nice. So, yes.

190
00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:11.160
You can wait for me
outside the door.

191
00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:16.540
And... I have to give 1000
to the club before I leave.

192
00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:28.510
And the 600 afterwards.

193
00:22:34.850 --> 00:22:36.430
See you outside.

194
00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:45.670
- Bitch! Damn it!
- Scumbag!

195
00:24:23.580 --> 00:24:26.710
What did you do with my money?
Give me back my money.

196
00:24:32.800 --> 00:24:34.590
Police.

197
00:24:35.640 --> 00:24:38.640
You come with me.
You two get lost.

198
00:24:38.720 --> 00:24:40.640
She stole my money.

199
00:24:41.810 --> 00:24:44.230
- Where are you taking me?
- Relax.

200
00:24:53.570 --> 00:24:56.700
Garage Girl!
Who are those foreign assholes?

201
00:24:57.530 --> 00:24:59.950
- What’s the problem?
- My neck hurts.

202
00:25:00.040 --> 00:25:02.870
Those son of a bitches
hurt your neck?

203
00:25:04.250 --> 00:25:06.170
Let me out, please.

204
00:25:06.250 --> 00:25:09.050
No. I’m taking you to a doctor first.

205
00:25:09.130 --> 00:25:11.130
Then I’ll get you home.

206
00:25:16.930 --> 00:25:18.720
I know a doctor nearby.

207
00:25:26.560 --> 00:25:29.270
Call the doctor.

208
00:25:29.360 --> 00:25:30.730
He’ll be here in a moment.

209
00:25:30.820 --> 00:25:32.740
Not in a moment. Now!

210
00:25:32.820 --> 00:25:37.280
I told you to call him now.
What’s your problem?

211
00:25:37.370 --> 00:25:38.740
Here he is.

212
00:25:38.830 --> 00:25:43.460
- Hi.
- Doctor, she fell on her neck.

213
00:25:44.080 --> 00:25:46.620
Okay, come on.

214
00:25:53.470 --> 00:25:55.800
- Did you really fall?
- Yes.

215
00:26:07.020 --> 00:26:09.020
Are you feeling better?

216
00:26:10.940 --> 00:26:12.780
A little.

217
00:26:15.490 --> 00:26:19.620
Tell me, do you have
a driver’s license?

218
00:26:21.870 --> 00:26:25.250
I think I might have a job for you.

219
00:26:25.330 --> 00:26:28.710
Just driving a car to the mountains
and back. It’s not far.

220
00:26:29.420 --> 00:26:32.630
I don’t smoke and I don’t drink.
I don’t like drugs.

221
00:26:32.710 --> 00:26:36.300
- This is work with cars.
- Give me a break.

222
00:26:36.880 --> 00:26:42.560
You just drive up to my farm,
my people are already there.

223
00:26:42.600 --> 00:26:46.600
Omar will show you everything.
There’s another girl...

224
00:26:49.730 --> 00:26:53.190
You drive up there and back.
That’s it.

225
00:26:54.110 --> 00:26:58.320
You’ll look nice,
a new car, new clothes.

226
00:26:59.160 --> 00:27:02.620
European license plates.
The police will never look at you twice.

227
00:27:02.700 --> 00:27:07.710
And if they question me?
Search me? I go to jail?

228
00:27:07.790 --> 00:27:12.090
What would they find? The car’s
empty, only clothes in your suitcase.

229
00:27:13.460 --> 00:27:15.050
I’m not that kind of girl.

230
00:27:15.130 --> 00:27:20.640
I know that.
But I’m talking about real money.

231
00:27:23.180 --> 00:27:26.060
8,000 dirhams, cash,
for one night.

232
00:27:27.230 --> 00:27:28.810
Use your pretty head.

233
00:27:32.690 --> 00:27:35.030
Please let me out here.

234
00:27:36.150 --> 00:27:38.530
You’re going to call me, right?

235
00:27:38.610 --> 00:27:41.660
I know you’re going to call me.

236
00:28:04.850 --> 00:28:07.020
So how can we raise some money?

237
00:28:10.060 --> 00:28:11.810
I get paid next week.

238
00:28:11.900 --> 00:28:14.150
And Norah is going to sell her laptop.

239
00:28:14.230 --> 00:28:17.230
That will make us 2,500 dirhams.

240
00:28:18.280 --> 00:28:20.490
That’s only one day of studio time.

241
00:28:21.360 --> 00:28:23.410
We’ll find a solution.

242
00:28:24.200 --> 00:28:25.450
How, Sarah?

243
00:28:25.830 --> 00:28:28.870
How are we going to find
two months of salary in three weeks?

244
00:28:28.950 --> 00:28:30.870
Calm down.

245
00:28:32.790 --> 00:28:35.710
What’s your problem?
Take it easy.

246
00:28:35.790 --> 00:28:37.710
Fuck take it easy.

247
00:28:38.460 --> 00:28:40.630
Do whatever you want.

248
00:28:40.720 --> 00:28:43.260
This is our chance
and I won’t miss it.

249
00:28:43.890 --> 00:28:46.890
Everybody is waiting in this country
and I’m tired of waiting.

250
00:29:04.700 --> 00:29:06.740
Hello? Mom?

251
00:29:32.430 --> 00:29:36.600
FINAL NOTICE BEFORE EVICTION

252
00:30:09.890 --> 00:30:11.930
Malika?

253
00:30:31.790 --> 00:30:33.950
What’s up? You okay?

254
00:30:34.040 --> 00:30:36.410
You’ve been in that drawer again, right?

255
00:30:37.420 --> 00:30:39.630
Not much money these days.

256
00:30:40.380 --> 00:30:43.130
I have to say,
you’ve always put it back.

257
00:30:44.300 --> 00:30:46.800
What are you going to do about the bank?

258
00:30:46.880 --> 00:30:50.970
The bank sends tough letters,
but they won’t take our apartment.

259
00:30:51.050 --> 00:30:52.100
No, Mama.

260
00:30:54.060 --> 00:30:55.890
Sarah’s uncle just lost his house.

261
00:30:56.520 --> 00:30:58.230
Why hasn’t Dad paid?

262
00:30:58.310 --> 00:31:00.860
You know the garage has been slow.

263
00:31:03.900 --> 00:31:07.450
There’s enough work.
What’s his problem?

264
00:31:09.910 --> 00:31:12.910
Your father was fine,
until two years ago...

265
00:31:12.990 --> 00:31:15.620
when the bank raised
the monthly payment.

266
00:31:16.200 --> 00:31:19.710
Now, he got lost somewhere.
He goes out, loses money.

267
00:31:19.790 --> 00:31:22.000
I’ve been paying
for everything for a long time.

268
00:31:22.090 --> 00:31:25.090
- What a hypocrite.
- Don’t talk that way about your father.

269
00:31:26.420 --> 00:31:29.930
You’re a child.
You don’t understand.

270
00:31:30.010 --> 00:31:31.930
You’re still defending him.

271
00:31:32.010 --> 00:31:33.680
He’s going to put you in the street.

272
00:31:34.890 --> 00:31:36.520
You could leave him.

273
00:31:44.980 --> 00:31:47.030
And Fatima?

274
00:31:51.950 --> 00:31:54.120
We’ll work it out.

275
00:31:54.200 --> 00:31:56.540
Don’t worry, Mom.

276
00:31:56.620 --> 00:31:59.160
I’m going to take a shower.
I’m exhausted.

277
00:32:32.110 --> 00:32:33.410
I need an advance.

278
00:32:33.990 --> 00:32:35.120
You want to go shopping?

279
00:33:07.480 --> 00:33:09.440
How is everything?

280
00:33:12.950 --> 00:33:14.950
Amal!

281
00:33:18.080 --> 00:33:19.240
Malika.

282
00:33:23.290 --> 00:33:25.210
She’s driving.

283
00:33:37.260 --> 00:33:39.810
We’ll be in the village in three hours.

284
00:33:53.190 --> 00:33:55.240
Malika, right?

285
00:33:55.950 --> 00:33:57.990
Yes, Malika.

286
00:33:59.330 --> 00:34:01.870
This is the anti-terrorist checkpoint.

287
00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:06.000
Be careful on your way back.

288
00:34:07.290 --> 00:34:10.000
If the cops stop you...

289
00:34:10.090 --> 00:34:11.460
you smile.

290
00:34:13.260 --> 00:34:15.260
You’re polite, respectful.

291
00:34:15.340 --> 00:34:17.890
You’re in a hurry like everyone else.

292
00:34:18.970 --> 00:34:21.220
I grew up here.

293
00:34:30.400 --> 00:34:32.030
Turn here.

294
00:34:32.690 --> 00:34:34.860
We go up the mountain.

295
00:34:53.210 --> 00:34:56.260
Don’t worry about these cops here.

296
00:34:57.340 --> 00:34:59.300
They only check for speeding.

297
00:34:59.390 --> 00:35:03.430
Always stay 10 kilometers
under the speed limit.

298
00:35:18.610 --> 00:35:20.120
Hello?

299
00:35:22.780 --> 00:35:24.790
We’re in Bab Berred.

300
00:35:26.160 --> 00:35:28.210
Well, I’m not the one driving.

301
00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:32.380
Darderra roadblock.

302
00:35:33.340 --> 00:35:35.960
The cops look for smugglers.

303
00:35:41.090 --> 00:35:42.140
Omar.

304
00:35:42.890 --> 00:35:44.600
What do you want?

305
00:35:45.270 --> 00:35:47.230
Whatever happened to Angaz?

306
00:35:47.310 --> 00:35:48.730
Who?

307
00:35:49.690 --> 00:35:52.150
The guy we used to work with?

308
00:35:52.230 --> 00:35:54.020
I don’t know who you’re talking about.

309
00:36:09.210 --> 00:36:11.040
Pull over there please.

310
00:36:22.300 --> 00:36:24.300
What now?

311
00:36:39.150 --> 00:36:41.030
Where are you from?

312
00:36:41.650 --> 00:36:43.280
Tangier.

313
00:36:43.870 --> 00:36:46.450
You’re a Tangerine?

314
00:36:48.290 --> 00:36:50.710
Never seen you in the bars or clubs.

315
00:36:51.620 --> 00:36:53.500
No, you haven’t.

316
00:36:56.340 --> 00:36:59.510
You better not mess up my game.

317
00:37:31.330 --> 00:37:33.040
What a dump.

318
00:37:33.120 --> 00:37:36.420
Don’t be fooled. Half the dope
in Europe comes through here.

319
00:37:45.470 --> 00:37:47.470
Turn here.

320
00:37:47.890 --> 00:37:49.930
Take a turn here and follow him.

321
00:38:12.790 --> 00:38:15.790
Be polite.
They are very nice people.

322
00:39:07.340 --> 00:39:09.970
50 kilos, four boxes.
How much?

323
00:39:11.140 --> 00:39:12.510
200.

324
00:39:13.560 --> 00:39:15.270
How much?

325
00:39:16.180 --> 00:39:17.390
200.

326
00:39:18.190 --> 00:39:21.770
Malika, time to learn.
Take apart that door.

327
00:39:37.410 --> 00:39:39.420
The knife first,
then the screwdriver.

328
00:39:41.420 --> 00:39:43.550
Do it softly.

329
00:39:43.630 --> 00:39:45.050
Good.

330
00:40:59.450 --> 00:41:01.210
Put some tape here.

331
00:41:10.880 --> 00:41:12.680
Good work.

332
00:41:14.640 --> 00:41:16.640
You’re a good girl.

333
00:41:17.470 --> 00:41:19.310
I can tell.

334
00:41:20.560 --> 00:41:24.560
Not like the street girls
who come here.

335
00:41:39.290 --> 00:41:41.750
Stop now. Go eat.

336
00:41:52.550 --> 00:41:55.890
- How is the food?
- It’s good. Thank you.

337
00:41:55.970 --> 00:41:59.760
Eat hearty, the road is long.

338
00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:27.420
Welcome from your journey, Haj.

339
00:42:35.340 --> 00:42:39.300
That door is packed.
Work on the rest.

340
00:43:18.680 --> 00:43:20.800
There’s a mattress
if you want to sleep.

341
00:43:22.640 --> 00:43:24.270
Thanks.

342
00:43:33.610 --> 00:43:36.190
We’re not supposed to go out.

343
00:44:20.410 --> 00:44:24.620
Next time,
I’ll show you the best view.

344
00:44:27.410 --> 00:44:29.500
Get some sleep,
you have an hour.

345
00:44:42.760 --> 00:44:44.350
Wake up.

346
00:44:47.180 --> 00:44:48.930
I’m awake.

347
00:45:08.580 --> 00:45:10.620
Put on these clothes.

348
00:45:15.460 --> 00:45:18.050
You work on cars like a man.

349
00:45:19.050 --> 00:45:20.920
That’s what my dad says.

350
00:45:21.010 --> 00:45:22.800
He never had a son.

351
00:45:23.930 --> 00:45:25.970
Do you have a boyfriend?

352
00:45:26.050 --> 00:45:27.970
Not at the moment.

353
00:45:29.720 --> 00:45:31.520
Why not?

354
00:45:31.600 --> 00:45:34.400
You are pretty enough.

355
00:45:35.360 --> 00:45:37.400
Not my priority.

356
00:45:38.320 --> 00:45:40.070
“Priority”?

357
00:45:40.150 --> 00:45:42.530
You are funny.

358
00:45:45.910 --> 00:45:48.280
I’ll show you my ex-boyfriend.

359
00:45:49.700 --> 00:45:51.710
Look, isn’t he cute?

360
00:45:55.960 --> 00:45:58.210
You know where we spent our holidays?

361
00:45:58.290 --> 00:45:59.920
Marbella!

362
00:46:00.590 --> 00:46:04.430
We had an apartment in Casablanca.
I was living with him.

363
00:46:05.340 --> 00:46:07.220
And then?

364
00:46:07.300 --> 00:46:09.510
We started to fight.

365
00:46:09.600 --> 00:46:12.140
He was hitting me too much.

366
00:46:12.230 --> 00:46:14.140
It was partly my fault.

367
00:46:15.150 --> 00:46:17.110
You’re better off without him.

368
00:46:17.190 --> 00:46:19.980
No, he was nice.
We had a lot of fun.

369
00:46:21.360 --> 00:46:23.280
Get in the car.

370
00:47:02.860 --> 00:47:04.820
What’s wrong with you?

371
00:47:05.570 --> 00:47:07.030
Nothing.

372
00:47:07.780 --> 00:47:10.700
- Are you tired?
- No, I’m fine.

373
00:47:13.620 --> 00:47:15.210
Look at me.

374
00:47:16.410 --> 00:47:19.000
- Are you sick?
- No, I’m okay.

375
00:47:22.460 --> 00:47:24.460
Listen to me.

376
00:47:25.050 --> 00:47:26.840
Stay on the main road.

377
00:47:26.880 --> 00:47:28.970
Don’t stop.

378
00:47:29.050 --> 00:47:30.100
Got me?

379
00:47:31.930 --> 00:47:32.930
Got me?

380
00:47:33.720 --> 00:47:35.930
First, go wash the car.

381
00:47:38.560 --> 00:47:40.560
We’ll be right behind you.

382
00:47:40.650 --> 00:47:42.400
Start the engine.

383
00:48:24.020 --> 00:48:26.230
Get out!

384
00:48:35.200 --> 00:48:37.040
What’s this? You sniffing?

385
00:48:37.750 --> 00:48:41.500
No, I didn’t touch your shipment.
I would never.

386
00:48:56.470 --> 00:49:00.060
You want the dogs to smell you?
Idiot!

387
00:49:25.130 --> 00:49:27.960
If the police stop you,
what do you say? What do you do?

388
00:49:28.050 --> 00:49:30.590
Be polite. Respectful. Smile.

389
00:49:30.670 --> 00:49:31.970
You.

390
00:49:33.550 --> 00:49:35.470
I’ve got my eye on you.

391
00:49:37.350 --> 00:49:39.430
Get out of here.

392
00:49:50.320 --> 00:49:52.030
I feel bad for you.

393
00:49:53.990 --> 00:49:56.700
- No worries.
- Who is that guy, Haj?

394
00:49:59.580 --> 00:50:01.960
Amal doesn’t know anything.

395
00:50:02.000 --> 00:50:05.330
The more you know,
the more problems you have.

396
00:50:16.640 --> 00:50:20.600
- I don’t see them.
- They stay two, three kilometers behind.

397
00:50:21.520 --> 00:50:23.980
If we get stopped...

398
00:50:24.060 --> 00:50:25.650
they’re not too close.

399
00:50:29.730 --> 00:50:33.650
- They follow us all the way to Tangier?
- All the way to the ferry port.

400
00:50:33.740 --> 00:50:37.160
What ferry port?
Nobody said anything about a ferry!

401
00:50:42.950 --> 00:50:46.170
You think we pack the car like this
to drive to Tangier?

402
00:50:47.330 --> 00:50:52.260
I have to drive this car to Paris.

403
00:50:55.470 --> 00:50:58.090
The Moroccans there
are really fucked up.

404
00:50:58.680 --> 00:51:02.020
Real gangsters.

405
00:51:04.270 --> 00:51:06.060
Don’t worry, Princess Malika...

406
00:51:06.600 --> 00:51:09.110
you’re getting out in Tangier.

407
00:51:12.070 --> 00:51:14.280
There’s also coke
in this car, isn’t there?

408
00:51:26.210 --> 00:51:29.670
The roadblock!

409
00:51:29.750 --> 00:51:31.540
Put on your seat belt.

410
00:51:46.230 --> 00:51:47.890
Good afternoon.

411
00:51:47.980 --> 00:51:49.980
- You weren’t wearing your seat belt.
- But I was.

412
00:51:50.940 --> 00:51:52.320
Registration.

413
00:52:01.490 --> 00:52:03.490
Her ID.

414
00:53:36.130 --> 00:53:38.050
We have to get back on the road.

415
00:53:38.130 --> 00:53:39.840
Did you eat something bad?

416
00:53:39.920 --> 00:53:43.220
Are you retarded?
We’re gonna go to jail.

417
00:53:44.180 --> 00:53:45.890
Nothing bad happened.

418
00:53:45.970 --> 00:53:48.350
Nothing bad happened?

419
00:53:49.020 --> 00:53:52.190
- Where are you going?
- You’re gonna get me thrown in jail.

420
00:53:52.230 --> 00:53:53.440
Me?

421
00:53:53.520 --> 00:53:55.520
Look at you!

422
00:53:55.610 --> 00:53:57.940
What’s the matter with me?

423
00:53:58.020 --> 00:54:00.820
Even with those clothes,
you look like a junky street girl!

424
00:54:02.320 --> 00:54:05.240
Shit. You all right? Sorry.

425
00:54:05.280 --> 00:54:08.410
We have to go. Now.
The other car is coming.

426
00:54:40.360 --> 00:54:42.360
I tried to get out, once.

427
00:54:48.370 --> 00:54:51.370
I went to the Spanish church in Tangier.

428
00:54:54.540 --> 00:54:57.290
I asked the nuns to help me.

429
00:54:58.380 --> 00:55:01.880
They were nice to me,
told me to come back tomorrow.

430
00:55:01.960 --> 00:55:06.010
The next morning, when I woke up,
there was a metal lock next to my head.

431
00:55:07.550 --> 00:55:10.680
I didn’t understand.
I took it when I went back to the nuns.

432
00:55:10.760 --> 00:55:12.560
They saw it and freaked out.

433
00:55:13.310 --> 00:55:16.310
Someone had stolen the lock off
the door of their church during the night.

434
00:55:16.350 --> 00:55:20.360
The nuns didn’t want anything
to do with me after that.

435
00:55:32.410 --> 00:55:37.580
For girls like us,
there’s only one way out.

436
00:55:40.590 --> 00:55:44.380
There was this other girl Aisha.
Pretty. She looked like you.

437
00:55:45.340 --> 00:55:47.340
She got to be Samir’s girl.

438
00:55:48.590 --> 00:55:52.430
He fell in love with her, gave
her a ring.

439
00:55:53.470 --> 00:55:56.390
One day she went on a run.

440
00:55:57.350 --> 00:55:59.400
There was a snitch.

441
00:55:59.480 --> 00:56:02.480
Cops stopped her in Darderra
and found cocaine.

442
00:56:05.150 --> 00:56:06.950
She went to jail.

443
00:56:08.150 --> 00:56:11.660
But just before her trial:
suicide.

444
00:56:14.120 --> 00:56:18.080
I used to go out with a prison guard.
He told me different.

445
00:56:19.870 --> 00:56:22.290
He told me
that she didn’t kill herself.

446
00:56:23.290 --> 00:56:26.420
They poisoned her.

447
00:56:28.510 --> 00:56:29.510
Samir?

448
00:56:30.340 --> 00:56:32.930
Samir knew she’d never snitch on him.

449
00:56:33.010 --> 00:56:37.020
She loved him.
He still wears her ring.

450
00:56:38.390 --> 00:56:40.400
Who then?

451
00:56:40.440 --> 00:56:43.650
It was Haj.

452
00:56:44.610 --> 00:56:47.440
He knew she’d talk about him.

453
00:56:47.530 --> 00:56:49.360
Does Samir know?

454
00:56:49.450 --> 00:56:51.410
Are you crazy?

455
00:57:17.060 --> 00:57:18.850
I look dead.

456
00:57:19.600 --> 00:57:21.730
You’re just scared and tired.

457
00:57:22.650 --> 00:57:24.440
I’m used to it.

458
00:57:24.480 --> 00:57:26.520
Used to fear.

459
00:57:28.900 --> 00:57:31.910
We’re like slaves for these assholes.

460
00:57:31.990 --> 00:57:34.620
I work, I get paid.

461
00:57:37.160 --> 00:57:39.580
It’s not a job if you can’t quit.

462
00:57:40.290 --> 00:57:42.290
It’s a prison.

463
00:57:42.750 --> 00:57:45.960
These people are not your family.
They’re devils.

464
00:57:48.340 --> 00:57:52.800
My mother always said,
“If you are a nail, endure the knocking.”

465
00:57:55.470 --> 00:57:57.430
That’s only half of that proverb.

466
00:57:58.100 --> 00:58:02.520
The other half says,
“If you are a hammer, strike.”

467
00:58:31.970 --> 00:58:33.970
Is that your sonogram?

468
00:58:36.800 --> 00:58:38.640
Can I see?

469
00:58:47.400 --> 00:58:49.360
Are you really pregnant?

470
00:58:57.160 --> 00:58:58.950
Have you seen a doctor since this?

471
00:59:01.910 --> 00:59:04.330
No.

472
00:59:15.680 --> 00:59:18.140
Amal, look at me.

473
00:59:20.180 --> 00:59:22.770
Do you want to keep this child?

474
00:59:28.520 --> 00:59:30.020
Yes.

475
00:59:34.400 --> 00:59:36.570
You have to get out of the country.

476
00:59:36.650 --> 00:59:37.950
It is your last chance.

477
00:59:38.030 --> 00:59:40.080
You can’t understand.

478
00:59:40.160 --> 00:59:42.910
If I ran away,
I could never come back–

479
00:59:42.990 --> 00:59:46.580
If you’re going to have your baby,
you can’t think about that.

480
00:59:46.620 --> 00:59:48.710
Get away from these assholes.

481
00:59:53.460 --> 00:59:55.800
You have a passport.

482
00:59:56.260 --> 01:00:00.600
The airport is right ahead.
You take the next flight to Europe.

483
01:00:00.680 --> 01:00:03.310
You vanish and never come back.

484
01:00:05.100 --> 01:00:08.310
If you stay, you’re going to die.

485
01:00:08.400 --> 01:00:09.770
You don’t understand.

486
01:00:09.850 --> 01:00:14.150
If I left, they would kill you.

487
01:00:14.230 --> 01:00:15.610
I’ll give back the car.

488
01:00:15.690 --> 01:00:18.820
If I run away, they’ll blame you.

489
01:00:20.820 --> 01:00:24.290
Samir never lets
any of the girls get away.

490
01:00:24.950 --> 01:00:26.960
I’m not like those girls.

491
01:00:41.720 --> 01:00:45.350
Road block must be slow today.

492
01:01:08.160 --> 01:01:10.000
Pretend you’re sick.

493
01:01:10.080 --> 01:01:12.710
Lean your head back.

494
01:01:21.300 --> 01:01:23.050
I’m so sorry sir.

495
01:01:23.140 --> 01:01:25.060
Please forgive me.
My friend is sick.

496
01:01:25.140 --> 01:01:29.430
She has an appointment
with Dr. Benani at Clinic Tingis.

497
01:01:30.390 --> 01:01:32.690
- What’s wrong, Missy?
- She’s really sick.

498
01:01:33.690 --> 01:01:35.900
I’m begging you, sir.
Please give us a break.

499
01:01:36.270 --> 01:01:38.320
What’s your problem?

500
01:02:33.790 --> 01:02:35.790
Show me your passport.

501
01:02:41.970 --> 01:02:43.970
You have an eyebrow pencil?

502
01:02:46.470 --> 01:02:48.260
Let your hair down.

503
01:02:51.100 --> 01:02:53.890
- You speak French, right?
- Yes. My cousin lives near–

504
01:02:54.940 --> 01:02:57.190
Don’t tell anyone where you are.

505
01:02:57.270 --> 01:02:58.860
Not even your mom.

506
01:02:58.940 --> 01:03:00.780
Fuck my mom.

507
01:03:01.990 --> 01:03:05.990
Hold your mouth shut.

508
01:03:06.070 --> 01:03:07.820
Like the girl in the picture.

509
01:03:07.910 --> 01:03:10.540
Take your passport.

510
01:03:11.910 --> 01:03:13.460
Hurry, go.

511
01:03:15.000 --> 01:03:18.840
- What if there are no seats on the plane?
- You’ll find one, hurry go now!

512
01:03:34.560 --> 01:03:36.850
It’s your chance. Take it.

513
01:03:45.570 --> 01:03:48.070
Amal is gone.
She can never come back.

514
01:03:48.160 --> 01:03:50.080
You’re someone else now.

515
01:03:53.660 --> 01:03:56.250
Go. Take care of your baby.

516
01:04:03.000 --> 01:04:05.010
You’ll need this. Good luck.

517
01:04:05.590 --> 01:04:07.220
There’s no such thing as luck.

518
01:06:29.230 --> 01:06:31.320
It’s Malika.

519
01:06:31.400 --> 01:06:33.490
I was in the gas station bathroom.

520
01:06:33.570 --> 01:06:35.910
When I came out, Amal was gone.
With the car.

521
01:06:35.990 --> 01:06:38.990
I looked everywhere.
What should I do now?

522
01:06:42.040 --> 01:06:45.170
I’m at the gas station
near the Marjane shopping center.

523
01:06:47.040 --> 01:06:48.460
Okay.

524
01:07:07.810 --> 01:07:09.270
Where’s the car?

525
01:07:09.360 --> 01:07:11.440
I don’t know.
All my stuff is in it.

526
01:07:11.530 --> 01:07:12.860
Where’s Amal?

527
01:07:14.110 --> 01:07:17.070
I don’t know. She was nervous
and sick the whole trip.

528
01:07:17.160 --> 01:07:19.370
Didn’t sleep, didn’t eat.

529
01:07:20.120 --> 01:07:22.790
When I came out of the bathroom,
she was gone.

530
01:07:22.870 --> 01:07:24.870
I called you so I could–
I’m sorry.

531
01:07:25.460 --> 01:07:28.380
Take off your glasses.

532
01:07:29.040 --> 01:07:30.420
Look at me.

533
01:07:30.500 --> 01:07:32.800
- Where’s Amal?
- I have no idea.

534
01:07:32.880 --> 01:07:34.630
She was complaining about the job.

535
01:07:35.050 --> 01:07:37.050
Where did she go?

536
01:07:37.140 --> 01:07:40.600
Maybe home to Marrakech. Her mother–
She had problems with her mother.

537
01:07:40.680 --> 01:07:42.020
The car?

538
01:07:42.060 --> 01:07:44.350
I don’t know.
I was in the toilets.

539
01:07:44.430 --> 01:07:47.400
- She was sniffing. It’s not my fault.
- Look at me.

540
01:07:47.480 --> 01:07:49.060
Where is my shit?

541
01:07:49.110 --> 01:07:52.730
Listen, I don’t know.
I don’t know where it is.

542
01:07:58.160 --> 01:08:01.120
Listen, motherfucker,
get on the Autoroute south.

543
01:08:01.200 --> 01:08:04.700
If you don’t catch her before Rabat,
follow the Marrakech road.

544
01:08:04.790 --> 01:08:06.120
Son of a bitch.

545
01:08:06.210 --> 01:08:09.710
- Why did you turn off after the checkpoint?
- Amal told me to go that way.

546
01:08:10.420 --> 01:08:12.630
If you’re lying...

547
01:08:12.710 --> 01:08:17.050
I swear I am going to kill you
and your fucking friend.

548
01:08:24.520 --> 01:08:26.940
- Where’s Amal?
- I don’t know.

549
01:08:27.020 --> 01:08:29.020
Where is she?

550
01:08:30.480 --> 01:08:34.690
I think you bitches are trying
to screw me.

551
01:08:35.820 --> 01:08:38.860
- Where’s the car?
- I wish I could tell you, but I don’t know.

552
01:08:39.450 --> 01:08:41.990
Try calling her again.

553
01:08:43.030 --> 01:08:44.370
Out of the service area.

554
01:08:49.670 --> 01:08:52.090
Today you die. Understand?

555
01:08:53.460 --> 01:08:57.340
Haj is about to come through that door.

556
01:08:57.420 --> 01:09:00.340
You better come up with some answers.

557
01:09:01.680 --> 01:09:04.100
- Where’s the car?
- I don’t know!

558
01:09:04.140 --> 01:09:07.310
Where’s Amal?
Where’s the car?

559
01:09:27.830 --> 01:09:29.210
Malika.

560
01:09:30.250 --> 01:09:34.420
We know each other, right?

561
01:09:36.800 --> 01:09:38.380
Malika Drissi.

562
01:09:38.470 --> 01:09:40.470
Your father Hassan lives in Branes.

563
01:09:41.220 --> 01:09:43.390
Your mother works at the Hotel Chamal.

564
01:09:46.350 --> 01:09:47.930
Where is the car?

565
01:09:48.730 --> 01:09:51.190
- I already told Samir everything–
- Slow down!

566
01:09:51.270 --> 01:09:52.850
- You know how much it’s worth–
- Hey.

567
01:09:53.770 --> 01:09:55.480
Immigrant.

568
01:09:56.360 --> 01:10:00.150
I don’t care about the car.
I don’t care about the money.

569
01:10:00.240 --> 01:10:01.820
I’m interested in the girl.

570
01:10:03.160 --> 01:10:04.870
Understand?

571
01:10:06.330 --> 01:10:08.830
Where’s the girl?

572
01:10:10.160 --> 01:10:11.540
I swear I don’t know.

573
01:10:11.620 --> 01:10:13.790
Call Amal again.

574
01:10:20.510 --> 01:10:22.050
Come here, Malika.

575
01:10:23.890 --> 01:10:25.470
Come here.

576
01:10:25.550 --> 01:10:27.260
Stand up.

577
01:10:35.980 --> 01:10:39.650
Can you help me find the girl?

578
01:10:41.400 --> 01:10:43.410
Because I won’t ask twice.

579
01:10:46.410 --> 01:10:48.620
Where is the car?

580
01:10:56.380 --> 01:11:02.300
I was just thinking: purse, my phone.
It was in the car.

581
01:11:04.380 --> 01:11:08.600
You could call it to reach Amal.

582
01:11:39.340 --> 01:11:42.460
Who is this?

583
01:11:44.220 --> 01:11:46.300
Where’s the girl?

584
01:11:46.380 --> 01:11:48.390
Answer me!

585
01:11:51.600 --> 01:11:55.440
Please. Let me call back.

586
01:12:12.370 --> 01:12:16.080
Sir, forgive me for bothering you...

587
01:12:16.670 --> 01:12:19.170
but I think you found my cell phone.

588
01:12:19.960 --> 01:12:22.550
I would like to meet you to thank you.

589
01:12:22.630 --> 01:12:24.760
Where are you, please?

590
01:12:25.300 --> 01:12:29.090
I know you didn’t steal it.
I just want to get it back.

591
01:12:30.470 --> 01:12:32.850
You’re at the bus station.

592
01:12:37.390 --> 01:12:40.520
- Take her with you.
- Let’s go!

593
01:13:35.120 --> 01:13:39.040
If the girl left on a bus,
maybe she left the car near here.

594
01:14:11.530 --> 01:14:13.490
Stop! There it is.

595
01:15:01.660 --> 01:15:03.920
I wanted to ask you something.

596
01:15:07.250 --> 01:15:09.250
This guy, Haj.

597
01:15:11.260 --> 01:15:13.760
He almost killed Amal up there.

598
01:15:14.680 --> 01:15:16.970
Did you know she’s pregnant?

599
01:15:20.560 --> 01:15:22.520
I need to tell you something about Haj.

600
01:15:23.980 --> 01:15:27.650
Amal told me about
a girl called Alia or Aisha.

601
01:15:27.730 --> 01:15:28.980
Aisha.

602
01:15:30.780 --> 01:15:33.610
She told me she committed
suicide in prison.

603
01:15:35.700 --> 01:15:39.200
But Amal heard from inside the prison.

604
01:15:40.080 --> 01:15:43.080
It was just made to look like a suicide.

605
01:15:47.380 --> 01:15:51.170
She said Haj had her killed.

606
01:15:54.670 --> 01:15:56.680
That’s all I know.

607
01:16:16.700 --> 01:16:18.780
Go.
